# Offline pin notes — gpw-hirshfeld-uks

## Method

Hirshfeld \(V/V_{\mathrm{free}}\) from the **Γ-UKS** GPW PBE total valence
density \(\rho=\rho_\alpha+\rho_\beta\) (in-tree exponential free-atom model,
`hirshfeld_tables.h`) → MBD@rsSCS with scaled α/C6/R (same libMBD free-atom
tables as `gpw-mbd-ice` / `gpw-mbd-hirshfeld`).

## Why not stock CP2K QS?

CP2K 2026.1 `PAIR_POTENTIAL TYPE` is only DFTD2|DFTD3|DFTD3(BJ)|DFTD4 — no
stock TS/MBD. Hard pin is the ATV product under fixed UKS settings (CUTOFF
200 Ry, DZVP-MOLOPT-GTH, GTH-PBE-q6, O₂ triplet Nα=7/Nβ=5, MT 12 Å cell),
cross-checked vs free-atom MBD and the dual in-tree Hirshfeld kernel.

## Geometry

Same centered O₂ as `gpw-uks-pbe` / `gpw-uks-o2-gamma` (R = 1.2075 Å).

## Pin (product settings)

```
E_disp = -1.0379964698969957e-04 Ha
volumes (O O) ≈ 0.6666 0.6666
CUTOFF 200 Ry, DZVP-MOLOPT-GTH, GTH-PBE-q6, O2 triplet Nα=7/Nβ=5, MT 12 Å
max_iter 150, tol 1e-6, mix 0.35, diis_depth 10
```
